1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,520
This is J. Krishnamurti's discussion with students in San Diego, California, 1970.

2
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:13,840
Krishnamurti What shall we talk over together this morning?

3
00:00:13,840 --> 00:00:22,240
This is supposed to be a discussion and I think the word discussion is not right.

4
00:00:23,240 --> 00:00:36,240
It is more a dialogue, exchange, not of opinions, because that will lead us nowhere.

5
00:00:36,240 --> 00:00:47,240
Or indulging in mere intellectual cleverness will have very little meaning.

6
00:00:48,240 --> 00:00:58,240
Because truth is not to be found through exchange of opinions or of ideas.

7
00:00:59,240 --> 00:01:10,240
So, if we are to talk over together any problem,

8
00:01:10,240 --> 00:01:20,240
it must be on the level which is not intellectual or emotional or sentimental,

9
00:01:20,240 --> 00:01:27,240
but problems that really affect one in one's daily living.

10
00:01:27,240 --> 00:01:32,240
And from there go into it. Yes, sir.

11
00:01:32,240 --> 00:01:36,240
Questioner I live in conflict with myself.

12
00:01:36,240 --> 00:01:39,240
I am a vegetarian from Rofnuda. I don't kill.

13
00:01:39,240 --> 00:01:44,240
But to solve the problem that communism takes not over,

14
00:01:44,240 --> 00:01:52,240
I think this war against communism is in a certain sense of self-mortgaging justified.

15
00:01:52,240 --> 00:01:57,240
I would like to find out with you if I am right or wrong.

16
00:01:57,240 --> 00:02:03,240
The gentleman says that he is a vegetarian, doesn't kill,

17
00:02:03,240 --> 00:02:10,240
and the fight against communism is self-protective response. Is that it, sir?

18
00:02:10,240 --> 00:02:13,240
Q. Yes.

19
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:19,240
K. That's really very funny.

20
00:02:19,240 --> 00:02:22,240
Q. You must understand, I lived ten years under communism.

21
00:02:22,240 --> 00:02:26,240
I was in a Russian concentration camp when I was in a communist prison.

22
00:02:26,240 --> 00:02:32,240
They understand only one language and it is power.

23
00:02:35,240 --> 00:02:38,240
K. So what is the question, sir?

24
00:02:38,240 --> 00:02:43,240
Q. The question is, is this war self-protection or not?

25
00:02:44,240 --> 00:02:49,240
K. I believe every war, every group that lead to war,

26
00:02:49,240 --> 00:02:52,240
the politicians that bring about wars,

27
00:02:52,240 --> 00:02:57,240
they always say, don't they, that it is self-protective war.

28
00:02:59,240 --> 00:03:04,240
Is that what you want to really discuss?

29
00:03:08,240 --> 00:03:15,240
Wars have always been, whether they are offensive or defensive, but they are wars.

30
00:03:16,240 --> 00:03:22,240
Killing each other has been a kind of peculiar, monstrous game

31
00:03:22,240 --> 00:03:25,240
throughout the centuries.

32
00:03:26,240 --> 00:03:32,240
And we are still, unfortunately, those so-called educated, cultured,

33
00:03:32,240 --> 00:03:38,240
still indulging in the most savage form of butchery.

34
00:03:39,240 --> 00:03:44,240
Could we go into the question of,

35
00:03:44,240 --> 00:03:49,240
if that is what interests some of you,

36
00:03:50,240 --> 00:03:57,240
what is deep violence, this aggression in man,

37
00:03:57,240 --> 00:04:01,240
and whether it is at all possible to be free of it?

38
00:04:01,240 --> 00:04:04,240
Could we discuss that?

39
00:04:08,240 --> 00:04:11,240
Do you really want to go into it?

40
00:04:12,240 --> 00:04:15,240
No?

41
00:04:21,240 --> 00:04:29,240
You know, there have been groups

42
00:04:29,240 --> 00:04:38,240
who have said that they will, under no circumstances, express violence,

43
00:04:39,240 --> 00:04:47,240
live a peaceful life, surrounded by people who are very aggressive, violent,

44
00:04:48,240 --> 00:04:59,240
a kind of nucleus amongst people who are savage, brutal, violent.

45
00:05:00,240 --> 00:05:03,240
And if one has observed,

46
00:05:04,240 --> 00:05:08,240
and if you'll forgive me talking about it a little bit about myself,

47
00:05:08,240 --> 00:05:11,240
I don't read books.

48
00:05:12,240 --> 00:05:16,240
I don't read, the speaker doesn't read the Gita,

49
00:05:16,240 --> 00:05:21,240
the Upanishads, the Bible, you know, all the philosophy and all that.

50
00:05:21,240 --> 00:05:25,240
But I think what is important is,

51
00:05:25,240 --> 00:05:30,240
if we could go into this deeply,

52
00:05:30,240 --> 00:05:34,240
into this question of aggression and violence,

53
00:05:34,240 --> 00:05:38,240
then perhaps it would be worthwhile

54
00:05:38,240 --> 00:05:45,240
and see how far the mind can be absolutely rid of this.

55
00:05:45,240 --> 00:05:48,240
Could we go into it?

56
00:05:52,240 --> 00:05:57,240
Because you see, I feel very strongly

57
00:05:59,240 --> 00:06:03,240
that there is no love in any form,

58
00:06:03,240 --> 00:06:10,240
if there is any spark or touch of violence in the mind.

59
00:06:12,240 --> 00:06:23,240
And how does the mind free itself of its accumulated violence,

60
00:06:25,240 --> 00:06:30,240
cultured violence, self-protective violence,

61
00:06:31,240 --> 00:06:35,240
the violence of aggression,

62
00:06:36,240 --> 00:06:39,240
the violence of competition,

63
00:06:40,240 --> 00:06:46,240
the violence of trying to be somebody,

64
00:06:47,240 --> 00:06:54,240
the violence of trying to discipline oneself according to a pattern.

65
00:06:55,240 --> 00:06:57,240
Please follow all this.

66
00:06:58,240 --> 00:07:02,240
Trying to become somebody,

67
00:07:02,240 --> 00:07:06,240
trying to suppress, trying to bully oneself,

68
00:07:06,240 --> 00:07:10,240
brutalise oneself in order to be,

69
00:07:10,240 --> 00:07:14,240
all such forms of violence,

70
00:07:15,240 --> 00:07:20,240
killing animals, killing the neighbour, killing the – you know.

71
00:07:20,240 --> 00:07:23,240
So,

72
00:07:24,240 --> 00:07:29,240
there are so many different kinds of violence.

73
00:07:31,240 --> 00:07:34,240
Shall we go into each violence,

74
00:07:35,240 --> 00:07:41,240
or shall we take the whole structure of violence?

75
00:07:43,240 --> 00:07:46,240
Not bit by bit.

76
00:07:47,240 --> 00:07:53,240
Can you look at the whole spectrum of violence?

77
00:07:56,240 --> 00:07:59,240
Not one part of it.

78
00:08:01,240 --> 00:08:04,240
Q. May I ask you the source?

79
00:08:04,240 --> 00:08:09,240
May I ask you what you feel is the source of violence?

80
00:08:09,240 --> 00:08:13,240
K. What is the source of violence?

81
00:08:16,240 --> 00:08:20,240
The source of violence is the me,

82
00:08:21,240 --> 00:08:25,240
the ego, the self,

83
00:08:27,240 --> 00:08:34,240
which expresses itself in so many ways,

84
00:08:35,240 --> 00:08:38,240
in division,

85
00:08:39,240 --> 00:08:42,240
in trust,

86
00:08:42,240 --> 00:08:45,240
in division,

87
00:08:46,240 --> 00:08:51,240
in trying to become or be somebody,

88
00:08:53,240 --> 00:08:59,240
in dividing the me and the not-me,

89
00:09:01,240 --> 00:09:07,240
the me that divides itself as the unconscious and the conscious,

90
00:09:08,240 --> 00:09:15,240
the me that identifies with the family and not the family,

91
00:09:16,240 --> 00:09:21,240
the community and not the community, and so on and on.

92
00:09:21,240 --> 00:09:26,240
It's like a drop of a stone in a lake,

93
00:09:26,240 --> 00:09:29,240
the waves spread, spread, spread,

94
00:09:29,240 --> 00:09:33,240
but the centre is the me.

95
00:09:38,240 --> 00:09:43,240
And as long as that in any form survives,

96
00:09:43,240 --> 00:09:49,240
very subtly or grossly, there must be violence.

97
00:09:51,240 --> 00:09:54,240
You see, you asked a question,

98
00:09:55,240 --> 00:09:59,240
what is the root cause of violence,

99
00:10:00,240 --> 00:10:05,240
but that is a question

100
00:10:05,240 --> 00:10:12,240
which by trying to find out what the cause is,

101
00:10:12,240 --> 00:10:16,240
we think we shall be rid of it.

102
00:10:17,240 --> 00:10:20,240
So shall we tackle that first thing?

103
00:10:20,240 --> 00:10:27,240
By thinking or enquiring into the cause of violence,

104
00:10:27,240 --> 00:10:32,240
we think we shall be able to get rid of it.

105
00:10:32,240 --> 00:10:35,240
Don't we?

106
00:10:38,240 --> 00:10:41,240
I say to myself, if I know why I am brutal,

107
00:10:41,240 --> 00:10:45,240
I have finished with brutality.

108
00:10:47,240 --> 00:10:54,240
And I spend weeks and months and years searching for the cause,

109
00:10:54,240 --> 00:11:00,240
or reading the explanations given by experts, specialists

110
00:11:00,240 --> 00:11:06,240
or specialists of the various causes of violence or aggression.

111
00:11:06,240 --> 00:11:08,240
But at the end of the volume,

112
00:11:08,240 --> 00:11:11,240
whether it's a small volume or ten volumes,

113
00:11:11,240 --> 00:11:14,240
I am still violent.

114
00:11:14,240 --> 00:11:17,240
Right?

115
00:11:19,240 --> 00:11:26,240
So, do we enquire into this question of violence

116
00:11:26,240 --> 00:11:32,240
through the discovery of the cause and the effect,

117
00:11:32,240 --> 00:11:38,240
or take the cause, the effect,

118
00:11:38,240 --> 00:11:43,240
and take the whole of it and look at it?

119
00:11:43,240 --> 00:11:49,240
Because the cause becomes the effect,

120
00:11:49,240 --> 00:11:53,240
and the effect becomes the cause.

121
00:11:53,240 --> 00:11:56,240
It's a chain process, isn't it?

122
00:11:56,240 --> 00:11:59,240
I don't know if you...

123
00:12:00,240 --> 00:12:07,240
There is no cause and effect so markedly different.

124
00:12:07,240 --> 00:12:10,240
It is a chain,

125
00:12:10,240 --> 00:12:13,240
a cause becoming the effect,

126
00:12:13,240 --> 00:12:18,240
and the effect becoming the cause.

127
00:12:18,240 --> 00:12:22,240
And we can go along this process indefinitely,

128
00:12:22,240 --> 00:12:27,240
but whereas if we could, I suggest,

129
00:12:27,240 --> 00:12:34,240
if we could look at this whole problem of violence in man

130
00:12:34,240 --> 00:12:37,240
and see how to resolve it, how to end it,

131
00:12:37,240 --> 00:12:43,240
how to put a... comprehend it so vitally that you come to an end.

132
00:12:43,240 --> 00:12:46,240
Could we do that?

133
00:12:53,240 --> 00:12:56,240
The me and the not me,

134
00:12:56,240 --> 00:12:59,240
is it the effect of the culture,

135
00:12:59,240 --> 00:13:03,240
the society in which we live,

136
00:13:03,240 --> 00:13:07,240
or is it innate,

137
00:13:07,240 --> 00:13:15,240
or is it born with us?

138
00:13:15,240 --> 00:13:20,240
Again, can you divide the culture from yourself and yourself

139
00:13:20,240 --> 00:13:22,240
from the society?

140
00:13:22,240 --> 00:13:27,240
Are they both the same, interrelated?

141
00:13:28,240 --> 00:13:35,240
The me, my greed, my problems, my desires, my anxieties,

142
00:13:35,240 --> 00:13:41,240
my fears, my hopes, my anguishing fulfilments and desires,

143
00:13:41,240 --> 00:13:48,240
my hopes, my anguishing fulfilments and despairs, deep sorrows,

144
00:13:48,240 --> 00:13:52,240
are also the product of my neighbour,

145
00:13:52,240 --> 00:13:56,240
of the community I live in.

146
00:13:56,240 --> 00:14:00,240
They are both interrelated, I cannot separate it

147
00:14:00,240 --> 00:14:05,240
and say, this is me and that is society.

148
00:14:05,240 --> 00:14:09,240
Once the separation has taken place,

149
00:14:09,240 --> 00:14:12,240
as in the case of most people,

150
00:14:12,240 --> 00:14:18,240
then this me becomes more self-centred, more active,

151
00:14:18,240 --> 00:14:23,240
more divisive and so on.

152
00:14:25,240 --> 00:14:28,240
So again we come to the question,

153
00:14:28,240 --> 00:14:32,240
can we take violence as a whole,

154
00:14:32,240 --> 00:14:35,240
including the me, which is the origin of violence,

155
00:14:35,240 --> 00:14:39,240
and the society in which we live is the origin of violence.

156
00:14:39,240 --> 00:14:44,240
Can we do that? Not separate it.

157
00:14:47,240 --> 00:14:51,240
We have built a society which is violent,

158
00:14:51,240 --> 00:14:55,240
and we, as human beings, are violent,

159
00:14:55,240 --> 00:14:58,240
and so the environment in which we live,

160
00:14:58,240 --> 00:15:03,240
the culture in which we live is the product of our endeavour,

161
00:15:03,240 --> 00:15:06,240
is the product of our struggle, of our pain,

162
00:15:06,240 --> 00:15:11,240
of our appalling brutalities.

163
00:15:15,240 --> 00:15:21,240
For me, the most important thing is,

164
00:15:22,240 --> 00:15:26,240
is it possible to end?

165
00:15:26,240 --> 00:15:32,240
Can one end this tremendous violence in one?

166
00:15:32,240 --> 00:15:36,240
That is really the question.

167
00:15:38,240 --> 00:15:43,240
Shall we do that? Can we discuss that?

168
00:15:44,240 --> 00:15:50,240
So don't let's go back to the cause again at the end of it.

169
00:15:50,240 --> 00:15:55,240
Q. Is it possible to transform by not eliminating or ending

170
00:15:55,240 --> 00:15:58,240
the sense of each other's intentions?

171
00:15:58,240 --> 00:16:05,240
K. Is it possible to transform it, not end it?

172
00:16:05,240 --> 00:16:09,240
We are going to find out.

173
00:16:09,240 --> 00:16:16,240
Because, look, violence is a form of energy.

174
00:16:20,240 --> 00:16:29,240
And that energy, utilised in a certain way, becomes aggression.

175
00:16:33,240 --> 00:16:39,240
So we are not trying to transform or change, but understand it,

176
00:16:39,240 --> 00:16:43,240
comprehend it so fully that one is free of it,

177
00:16:43,240 --> 00:16:46,240
the mind has gone beyond it,

178
00:16:46,240 --> 00:16:50,240
whether it has transcended it or transformed it and ended it,

179
00:16:50,240 --> 00:16:52,240
that is irrelevant.

180
00:16:52,240 --> 00:16:55,240
Those are verbal means of communication.

181
00:16:55,240 --> 00:16:59,240
So can we discuss this?

182
00:17:00,240 --> 00:17:06,240
Is it possible – not possible, it is possible –

183
00:17:06,240 --> 00:17:10,240
these words –

184
00:17:10,240 --> 00:17:23,240
to enquire together into this question of violence and going beyond it?

185
00:17:24,240 --> 00:17:27,240
Shall we do this, sir? Yes, sir?

186
00:17:28,240 --> 00:17:35,240
Q. If our action, which we say is the effect, is the act of violence,

187
00:17:35,240 --> 00:17:44,240
then the cause is violence in us, which the action is an expression of.

188
00:17:44,240 --> 00:17:52,240
Now, we are violent and the me is violent,

189
00:17:52,240 --> 00:17:58,240
so what is that doing for the me, for me to be violent?

190
00:17:58,240 --> 00:18:03,240
What is that thing that is being expressed when I am violent?

191
00:18:04,240 --> 00:18:08,240
K. I see what you mean, sir. Is this what you mean?

192
00:18:08,240 --> 00:18:11,240
And please correct it.

193
00:18:14,240 --> 00:18:23,240
The me is, we said, the centre of violence.

194
00:18:24,240 --> 00:18:28,240
How does that me come into being,

195
00:18:29,240 --> 00:18:35,240
which then protects itself in order to survive,

196
00:18:35,240 --> 00:18:40,240
and in the protection of itself, in the security of itself,

197
00:18:40,240 --> 00:18:46,240
it must bring about violence?

198
00:18:49,240 --> 00:18:55,240
So you are asking, how does this me come about?

199
00:18:56,240 --> 00:19:01,240
Which is the very centre of aggression.

200
00:19:01,240 --> 00:19:05,240
And aggression is the effect of the me

201
00:19:05,240 --> 00:19:13,240
who is separating itself from the you

202
00:19:15,240 --> 00:19:18,240
and therefore resisting you,

203
00:19:18,240 --> 00:19:23,240
and therefore becoming aggressive.

204
00:19:23,240 --> 00:19:28,240
So you are asking, are you not, sir,

205
00:19:29,240 --> 00:19:33,240
how does the me come into being,

206
00:19:33,240 --> 00:19:41,240
and if that is the cause of all violence in humanity,

207
00:19:43,240 --> 00:19:50,240
then the very transformation of the me

208
00:19:51,240 --> 00:19:55,240
will end all violence.

209
00:19:55,240 --> 00:20:00,240
That is what we are trying to find out,

210
00:20:00,240 --> 00:20:04,240
to enquire into the ending

211
00:20:04,240 --> 00:20:09,240
or drying up the source of aggression.

212
00:20:09,240 --> 00:20:11,240
Now let's proceed, sir, let's get going,

213
00:20:11,240 --> 00:20:16,240
otherwise we can go on verbalisation forever.

214
00:20:16,240 --> 00:20:26,240
Now, how do we grapple with this question?

215
00:20:29,240 --> 00:20:37,240
Abstractly or directly realising that human beings are violent.

216
00:20:37,240 --> 00:20:41,240
How do you think about violence?

217
00:20:41,240 --> 00:20:43,240
How do you look at violence?

218
00:20:43,240 --> 00:20:49,240
Do you look at violence in another or violence in yourself?

219
00:20:49,240 --> 00:20:53,240
Please do watch it, please listen to the question.

220
00:20:53,240 --> 00:20:58,240
How do you know you are violent?

221
00:21:07,240 --> 00:21:11,240
Conflict is violence.

222
00:21:11,240 --> 00:21:17,240
And when there is conflict, is one aware that one is violent?

223
00:21:17,240 --> 00:21:23,240
How do you know violence?

224
00:21:25,240 --> 00:21:31,240
This is really a complex question, knowing.

225
00:21:32,240 --> 00:21:40,240
Look, sir, when I say, I know you,

226
00:21:40,240 --> 00:21:44,240
what does that mean, I know?

227
00:21:44,240 --> 00:21:50,240
I know you as you were yesterday when I met you,

228
00:21:50,240 --> 00:21:54,240
or ten years ago when I met you.

229
00:21:54,240 --> 00:21:58,240
But between ten years ago and now,

230
00:21:58,240 --> 00:22:00,240
you might have changed and I might have changed,

231
00:22:00,240 --> 00:22:04,240
therefore I don't know you.

232
00:22:04,240 --> 00:22:09,240
I know you only ten years ago or ten days ago,

233
00:22:09,240 --> 00:22:13,240
therefore I can never say I know you.

234
00:22:13,240 --> 00:22:20,240
Do please understand this simple thing first.

235
00:22:20,240 --> 00:22:23,240
Therefore I can never say,

236
00:22:23,240 --> 00:22:26,240
I can always say I have been violent,

237
00:22:26,240 --> 00:22:29,240
but I don't know what violence now is.

238
00:22:29,240 --> 00:22:33,240
You understand what I am talking?

239
00:22:33,240 --> 00:22:38,240
Are we...

240
00:22:38,240 --> 00:22:43,240
So how do you know violence

241
00:22:43,240 --> 00:22:47,240
when you say, I am violent, I am angry,

242
00:22:47,240 --> 00:22:51,240
I hate somebody – I hope you don't –

243
00:22:51,240 --> 00:22:58,240
but when you say these things, what do you mean by it?

244
00:22:58,240 --> 00:23:03,240
Right?

245
00:23:09,240 --> 00:23:18,240
Look, sir, I am angry.

246
00:23:18,240 --> 00:23:22,240
You say something to me which irritates my nerves

247
00:23:22,240 --> 00:23:27,240
and all the rest of the organical process,

248
00:23:27,240 --> 00:23:30,240
I am angry.

249
00:23:30,240 --> 00:23:33,240
And then I say afterwards, second later,

250
00:23:33,240 --> 00:23:37,240
I say, by Jove, I have been angry.

251
00:23:37,240 --> 00:23:41,240
At the moment of anger I don't recognise it,

252
00:23:41,240 --> 00:23:44,240
only later I recognise it.

253
00:23:44,240 --> 00:23:47,240
Now, the recognition,

254
00:23:47,240 --> 00:23:53,240
you have to examine the structure of recognition,

255
00:23:53,240 --> 00:23:59,240
because if you don't understand the structure of recognition

256
00:23:59,240 --> 00:24:04,240
you won't be able to meet anger afresh.

257
00:24:04,240 --> 00:24:06,240
I don't know if you...

258
00:24:06,240 --> 00:24:13,240
Look, I am angry,

259
00:24:13,240 --> 00:24:18,240
and I realise I am angry a moment later.

260
00:24:18,240 --> 00:24:24,240
The realisation is the recognition, I have been angry.

261
00:24:24,240 --> 00:24:31,240
The recognition takes place when I have been angry before,

262
00:24:31,240 --> 00:24:34,240
otherwise I don't know it is anger.

263
00:24:34,240 --> 00:24:38,240
So when I recognise it,

264
00:24:38,240 --> 00:24:42,240
I recognise it only because I have known it before.

265
00:24:42,240 --> 00:24:46,240
See what has happened.

266
00:24:46,240 --> 00:24:52,240
The past interferes with the present,

267
00:24:52,240 --> 00:24:57,240
and then I say I am angry.

268
00:24:57,240 --> 00:25:02,240
So I am always translating the present reaction

269
00:25:02,240 --> 00:25:05,240
in terms of the past.

270
00:25:05,240 --> 00:25:15,240
So can I, without translating the present response with the past,

271
00:25:15,240 --> 00:25:19,240
can I look at the response anew,

272
00:25:19,240 --> 00:25:23,240
you understand, with a fresh mind?

273
00:25:23,240 --> 00:25:27,240
Are we meeting each other?

274
00:25:27,240 --> 00:25:31,240
No, please do it.

275
00:25:31,240 --> 00:25:36,240
Look, you call me a fool,

276
00:25:37,240 --> 00:25:42,240
and my whole blood, every thing,

277
00:25:42,240 --> 00:25:48,240
comes to the surface and says, you are another.

278
00:25:50,240 --> 00:25:59,240
And what has taken place in me, emotionally, inwardly?

279
00:25:59,240 --> 00:26:04,240
I have an image about myself.

280
00:26:04,240 --> 00:26:09,240
And that image says, I am not a fool,

281
00:26:09,240 --> 00:26:12,240
I have made that image into something

282
00:26:12,240 --> 00:26:15,240
which I think is desirable, noble, worthwhile,

283
00:26:15,240 --> 00:26:19,240
and you are insulting that image.

284
00:26:19,240 --> 00:26:25,240
And that image responds, which is the old.

285
00:26:25,240 --> 00:26:28,240
You are following?

286
00:26:28,240 --> 00:26:34,240
And so the old responds.

287
00:26:34,240 --> 00:26:39,240
So the next question is, can the response,

288
00:26:39,240 --> 00:26:45,240
can the response not be related to the old,

289
00:26:45,240 --> 00:26:51,240
therefore an interval between the old and the new response?

290
00:26:51,240 --> 00:26:54,240
You follow?

291
00:26:54,240 --> 00:27:01,240
Can the old be dormant, be hesitant,

292
00:27:01,240 --> 00:27:06,240
so as to allow the new to take place?

293
00:27:06,240 --> 00:27:09,240
You understand?

294
00:27:11,240 --> 00:27:17,240
I think that is where the whole problem is.

295
00:27:18,240 --> 00:27:24,240
I think that is where the whole problem is.

296
00:27:26,240 --> 00:27:29,240
Q. Are you saying then that violence, the root of violence,

297
00:27:29,240 --> 00:27:33,240
all violence is just confusion of what isn't and what is?

298
00:27:33,240 --> 00:27:37,240
K. No, sir, no, sir, no, sir.

299
00:27:37,240 --> 00:27:41,240
Look, let's begin again.

300
00:27:42,240 --> 00:27:46,240
We are violent.

301
00:27:46,240 --> 00:27:50,240
Throughout man's existence,

302
00:27:50,240 --> 00:27:54,240
human beings have been violent and are violent.

303
00:27:55,240 --> 00:27:59,240
I want to find out as a human being

304
00:27:59,240 --> 00:28:05,240
how to transcend this violence, how to go beyond it.

305
00:28:07,240 --> 00:28:11,240
What am I to do?

306
00:28:12,240 --> 00:28:19,240
Because I see what violence has done in the world,

307
00:28:22,240 --> 00:28:26,240
how it has destroyed every form of friendship,

308
00:28:26,240 --> 00:28:30,240
every form of relationship,

309
00:28:30,240 --> 00:28:36,240
how it has brought deep agony in oneself, misery.

310
00:28:36,240 --> 00:28:38,240
I see all that.

311
00:28:38,240 --> 00:28:41,240
And I say to myself,

312
00:28:41,240 --> 00:28:45,240
I want to live really a peaceful life

313
00:28:45,240 --> 00:28:48,240
in which there is deep abundance of love,

314
00:28:48,240 --> 00:28:53,240
and the violence must disappear, or must go, etc.

315
00:28:53,240 --> 00:28:57,240
Now, what am I to do?

316
00:29:00,240 --> 00:29:04,240
First, I mustn't escape from it.

317
00:29:04,240 --> 00:29:07,240
Right?

318
00:29:08,240 --> 00:29:10,240
Let's be sure of that.

319
00:29:10,240 --> 00:29:15,240
I must not escape from the fact I am violent.

320
00:29:15,240 --> 00:29:20,240
Escaping being, condemning it.

321
00:29:20,240 --> 00:29:23,240
Right?

322
00:29:24,240 --> 00:29:27,240
Justifying it,

323
00:29:27,240 --> 00:29:31,240
or even naming that I am violent.

324
00:29:32,240 --> 00:29:33,240
You are following?

325
00:29:33,240 --> 00:29:38,240
Because the naming is a form of condemnation,

326
00:29:41,240 --> 00:29:44,240
is a form of justification.

327
00:29:44,240 --> 00:29:48,240
So, first I have to realise

328
00:29:48,240 --> 00:29:55,240
the mind must not be distracted from this fact of violence,

329
00:29:55,240 --> 00:30:00,240
either in seeking the cause

330
00:30:00,240 --> 00:30:05,240
or in the explanation of the cause,

331
00:30:05,240 --> 00:30:09,240
or naming the fact that I am violent,

332
00:30:09,240 --> 00:30:13,240
or justifying it, condemning it, trying to get rid of it.

333
00:30:13,240 --> 00:30:16,240
Those are all forms of distraction

334
00:30:16,240 --> 00:30:21,240
from the fact of violence. Right?

335
00:30:23,240 --> 00:30:25,240
This is clear, is it?

336
00:30:25,240 --> 00:30:31,240
So, the mind must be absolutely clear

337
00:30:31,240 --> 00:30:35,240
that there is no escape from it.

338
00:30:38,240 --> 00:30:42,240
Not the exercise of will, who says, I will conquer it,

339
00:30:42,240 --> 00:30:47,240
because will is the very essence of violence.

340
00:30:48,240 --> 00:30:51,240
I don't know if you are...

341
00:30:51,240 --> 00:30:55,240
Q. Are we trying to find some order in it, order in the violence?

342
00:30:55,240 --> 00:30:56,240
K. What, sir?

343
00:30:56,240 --> 00:30:58,240
Q. Order in why we are violent?

344
00:30:58,240 --> 00:31:03,240
K. Are we trying to bring order into violence? Is that it?

345
00:31:03,240 --> 00:31:06,240
Q. Well, basically, are we trying to find what violence is

346
00:31:06,240 --> 00:31:10,240
by finding order in it, or the order in ourselves?

347
00:31:10,240 --> 00:31:15,240
K. No, sir, no, sir. How can there be order in violence?

348
00:31:15,240 --> 00:31:18,240
Violence is disorder.

349
00:31:18,240 --> 00:31:21,240
Do please go with me a little bit.

350
00:31:21,240 --> 00:31:27,240
First, no escape from it, of any kind,

351
00:31:27,240 --> 00:31:34,240
intellectual, explanatory, justification.

352
00:31:34,240 --> 00:31:37,240
See the difficulty of this,

353
00:31:37,240 --> 00:31:44,240
because our mind is so cunning, so sharp to escape,

354
00:31:44,240 --> 00:31:48,240
because it doesn't know what to do with it.

355
00:31:48,240 --> 00:31:51,240
It is not capable of dealing with it,

356
00:31:51,240 --> 00:31:57,240
or it thinks it is not capable, therefore it escapes.

357
00:31:57,240 --> 00:32:05,240
Look, sir, most of us know what loneliness is, don't we?

358
00:32:05,240 --> 00:32:10,240
Don't you? Being lonely.

359
00:32:11,240 --> 00:32:15,240
And being lonely, not knowing what to do with it,

360
00:32:15,240 --> 00:32:19,240
being afraid of it, we move away from it.

361
00:32:19,240 --> 00:32:24,240
Right? We escape from it.

362
00:32:28,240 --> 00:32:31,240
Or try to fill that emptiness by knowledge,

363
00:32:31,240 --> 00:32:34,240
by all kinds of things.

364
00:32:34,240 --> 00:32:40,240
All those are distractions from the fact of loneliness.

365
00:32:41,240 --> 00:32:47,240
Right? And therefore it is still there.

366
00:32:47,240 --> 00:32:55,240
So what one has to realise first is not to escape.

367
00:32:56,240 --> 00:33:02,240
Realise that every form of escape, distraction,

368
00:33:02,240 --> 00:33:11,240
a movement away, only sustains violence.

369
00:33:14,240 --> 00:33:20,240
So the mind then is confronted with the fact,

370
00:33:20,240 --> 00:33:23,240
with what is, and nothing else.

371
00:33:23,240 --> 00:33:25,240
Right?

372
00:33:26,240 --> 00:33:28,240
Are we doing this, please?

373
00:33:28,240 --> 00:33:32,240
This is a discussion, not a talk by me.

374
00:33:32,240 --> 00:33:38,240
Q. The thought of loneliness, it's felt that if you say it and I hear it,

375
00:33:38,240 --> 00:33:40,240
and I say to myself, I am lonely,

376
00:33:40,240 --> 00:33:44,240
I immediately feel that I have escaped in saying that.

377
00:33:44,240 --> 00:33:48,240
K. Of course, of course you have escaped when you say, I am lonely.

378
00:33:48,240 --> 00:33:53,240
You know the fact of loneliness, you know what it means.

379
00:33:54,240 --> 00:33:57,240
Don't you?

380
00:33:57,240 --> 00:34:01,240
Look, sir, it's so simple.

381
00:34:06,240 --> 00:34:09,240
Look, sir, when you look at a tree – do watch it –

382
00:34:09,240 --> 00:34:13,240
when you look at a tree, if you say, what a beautiful tree that is,

383
00:34:13,240 --> 00:34:19,240
your mind has already gone away from observing the tree, isn't it?

384
00:34:19,240 --> 00:34:22,240
No?

385
00:34:23,240 --> 00:34:28,240
So to look at the tree is not to say it's a beautiful tree.

386
00:34:30,240 --> 00:34:34,240
Therefore your attention is completely looking.

387
00:34:34,240 --> 00:34:37,240
Right?

388
00:34:39,240 --> 00:34:43,240
So when you say, what a beautiful river that is,

389
00:34:43,240 --> 00:34:48,240
what a lovely view that is, you have already gone.

390
00:34:53,240 --> 00:34:57,240
Yes, sir, yes. Behind you, sir, behind.

391
00:34:57,240 --> 00:35:00,240
Q. So whether it's violence or loneliness, you don't name it.

392
00:35:00,240 --> 00:35:02,240
K. We are going to find out, sir.

393
00:35:02,240 --> 00:35:08,240
Do it, sir, do it, and you will have answered it yourself.

394
00:35:08,240 --> 00:35:15,240
When you name it, you are relating it, the name, to the past.

395
00:35:15,240 --> 00:35:18,240
Therefore you are looking at it

396
00:35:18,240 --> 00:35:22,240
with the eyes that have been touched by the past.

397
00:35:22,240 --> 00:35:28,240
Therefore you are not looking at it afresh. That's all.

398
00:35:28,240 --> 00:35:31,240
You get the point?

399
00:35:33,240 --> 00:35:36,240
You look at violence – please do listen to this –

400
00:35:36,240 --> 00:35:43,240
you look at violence with eyes that have condemned,

401
00:35:43,240 --> 00:35:47,240
that are conditioned, that are justifying,

402
00:35:47,240 --> 00:35:52,240
that say violence is necessary to live in this monstrous society,

403
00:35:52,240 --> 00:35:58,240
violence is part of nature, part – look, nature kills, and so on.

404
00:35:58,240 --> 00:35:59,240
You follow?

405
00:35:59,240 --> 00:36:04,240
With the eyes that are conditioned to look,

406
00:36:04,240 --> 00:36:10,240
with condemnation or justification or resistance,

407
00:36:10,240 --> 00:36:16,240
what we are saying is to look at it afresh,

408
00:36:17,240 --> 00:36:21,240
anew, and you can only do that when you become aware

409
00:36:21,240 --> 00:36:30,240
that you are identifying what you see with what you already know,

410
00:36:30,240 --> 00:36:35,240
and therefore not looking at it afresh. Right?

411
00:36:35,240 --> 00:36:39,240
Just get this point, please.

412
00:36:40,240 --> 00:36:45,240
Just a minute, sir, your turn will come. Just a minute, sir.

413
00:36:47,240 --> 00:36:57,240
Look, sir, I look at my wife or my husband – I'm not married –

414
00:36:57,240 --> 00:37:01,240
I look at my wife or my husband.

415
00:37:02,240 --> 00:37:07,240
Do I ever really look at her or him,

416
00:37:07,240 --> 00:37:14,240
or do I look at her with the image that I have so carefully built

417
00:37:14,240 --> 00:37:20,240
for 30, 40, 50 years, or 10 days,

418
00:37:23,240 --> 00:37:27,240
and she does the same with me?

419
00:37:28,240 --> 00:37:34,240
And therefore our relationship is between the images

420
00:37:34,240 --> 00:37:38,240
and not actual relationship.

421
00:37:38,240 --> 00:37:41,240
You are following this?

422
00:37:41,240 --> 00:37:46,240
Do you? If you do, then break the image.

423
00:37:53,240 --> 00:37:56,240
So the question then arises,

424
00:37:57,240 --> 00:38:02,240
how is the image formed,

425
00:38:02,240 --> 00:38:07,240
what is the mechanism that forms images?

426
00:38:07,240 --> 00:38:16,240
Q. There is a space between your perception and your response.

427
00:38:16,240 --> 00:38:18,240
That would be time, I suppose.

428
00:38:18,240 --> 00:38:23,240
K. Yes, sir, that's right, but go into it a little more, you will see it.

429
00:38:25,240 --> 00:38:29,240
My wife says to me, you are an ass.

430
00:38:32,240 --> 00:38:35,240
I don't like it.

431
00:38:36,240 --> 00:38:42,240
And that has left a mark on my mind.

432
00:38:43,240 --> 00:38:48,240
Do this, sir, you have left a mark on my mind.

433
00:38:49,240 --> 00:38:53,240
And she says something else, that also leaves a mark on my mind.

434
00:38:53,240 --> 00:38:58,240
So these marks are the images.

435
00:38:58,240 --> 00:39:03,240
Now when she says to me, I am a fool,

436
00:39:03,240 --> 00:39:08,240
if I am aware at that minute – you understand? – aware,

437
00:39:08,240 --> 00:39:15,240
give attention, then there is no marking at all.

438
00:39:15,240 --> 00:39:20,240
You follow it? Because she may be right.

439
00:39:20,240 --> 00:39:25,240
Therefore I am attentive, watching.

440
00:39:25,240 --> 00:39:31,240
So inattention breeds images.

441
00:39:31,240 --> 00:39:37,240
Attention frees the mind from the image. Got this?

442
00:39:38,240 --> 00:39:42,240
You understand, sir? This is very simple.

443
00:39:42,240 --> 00:39:47,240
In the same way, when I am angry,

444
00:39:47,240 --> 00:39:51,240
when I am angry,

445
00:39:52,240 --> 00:39:55,240
to be completely attentive,

446
00:39:55,240 --> 00:39:59,240
not let inattention come in,

447
00:39:59,240 --> 00:40:05,240
which is to allow the past to come and interfere

448
00:40:05,240 --> 00:40:09,240
with the actual perception of anger at the moment.

449
00:40:09,240 --> 00:40:12,240
Got it?

450
00:40:12,240 --> 00:40:15,240
Right?

451
00:40:16,240 --> 00:40:20,240
Q. Is that not an act of will? K. No, we said that.

452
00:40:20,240 --> 00:40:23,240
Is that not an act of will?

453
00:40:23,240 --> 00:40:28,240
We said will is in essence violence.

454
00:40:28,240 --> 00:40:32,240
You know what? Wait a minute, let's examine what will is.

455
00:40:32,240 --> 00:40:35,240
What is will?

456
00:40:35,240 --> 00:40:39,240
I want to do that, I won't have that,

457
00:40:39,240 --> 00:40:42,240
I shall do that.

458
00:40:44,240 --> 00:40:50,240
I have resisted, I demand – will, desire.

459
00:40:52,240 --> 00:40:54,240
Which is what?

460
00:40:54,240 --> 00:40:57,240
Which is a form of resistance, isn't it?

461
00:40:57,240 --> 00:41:00,240
When you say, I will that,

462
00:41:00,240 --> 00:41:02,240
it is a form of resistance.

463
00:41:02,240 --> 00:41:06,240
And resistance is violence.

464
00:41:09,240 --> 00:41:11,240
Yes, sir?

465
00:41:11,240 --> 00:41:15,240
Q. Can you suggest a way of going about

466
00:41:15,240 --> 00:41:19,240
answering the questions which you raise?

467
00:41:19,240 --> 00:41:24,240
I refer to, number one,

468
00:41:24,240 --> 00:41:29,240
your comments that it is better to be aware

469
00:41:29,240 --> 00:41:31,240
than to rationalise.

470
00:41:31,240 --> 00:41:33,240
Perhaps I am paraphrasing you wrong,

471
00:41:33,240 --> 00:41:38,240
but as soon as you use words to rationalise

472
00:41:38,240 --> 00:41:42,240
and try to determine an answer,

473
00:41:42,240 --> 00:41:46,240
you are defeating your own attempts

474
00:41:46,240 --> 00:41:52,240
to arrive at an answer to the questions that you raise.

475
00:41:52,240 --> 00:41:55,240
K. I don't quite follow, sir.

476
00:41:55,240 --> 00:41:58,240
Q. I am asking possibly

477
00:41:58,240 --> 00:42:02,240
if there is some non-verbal internal communication

478
00:42:02,240 --> 00:42:05,240
that you are referring to

479
00:42:05,240 --> 00:42:11,240
in order to answer some of the questions that you ask.

480
00:42:13,240 --> 00:42:15,240
K. I don't quite understand this.

481
00:42:15,240 --> 00:42:17,240
Wait a minute, sir.

482
00:42:17,240 --> 00:42:20,240
Q. I was going to say what he is saying.

483
00:42:20,240 --> 00:42:23,240
Is there – if I may say so.

484
00:42:23,240 --> 00:42:25,240
Q. Go right ahead. I hope so.

485
00:42:25,240 --> 00:42:29,240
I hope you can describe it better than I do.

486
00:42:29,240 --> 00:42:33,240
Q. What you are saying is the what is,

487
00:42:33,240 --> 00:42:37,240
and then there is the response to the what is, which is the memory.

488
00:42:37,240 --> 00:42:39,240
Now he is saying,

489
00:42:39,240 --> 00:42:43,240
is there something else besides the memory of the past

490
00:42:43,240 --> 00:42:50,240
in which there is a non-verbal communication of knowing?

491
00:42:50,240 --> 00:42:58,240
Is there another way of knowing other than being the past?

492
00:42:58,240 --> 00:43:01,240
Is there another communication, another...?

493
00:43:01,240 --> 00:43:10,240
Are you trying to say, ask, sir, is there a communion which is non-verbal?

494
00:43:12,240 --> 00:43:15,240
Q. I guess what I am really trying to say is

495
00:43:15,240 --> 00:43:19,240
that you are trying to talk to something that is in the essence

496
00:43:19,240 --> 00:43:22,240
within a person, within each one of us.

497
00:43:22,240 --> 00:43:25,240
K. No, sir, I don't know...

498
00:43:25,240 --> 00:43:28,240
Q. Maybe I am...

499
00:43:28,240 --> 00:43:31,240
Q. Is there a time to describe that which is indescribable?

500
00:43:31,240 --> 00:43:32,240
Is that not it?

501
00:43:32,240 --> 00:43:35,240
K. No, sir, don't let's go off, please.

502
00:43:35,240 --> 00:43:39,240
I am trying to... Look, we are trying to find out

503
00:43:39,240 --> 00:43:45,240
whether violence can end.

504
00:43:45,240 --> 00:43:48,240
That's all. Don't let's go off to something else.

505
00:43:48,240 --> 00:43:50,240
May I take my coat off?

506
00:43:50,240 --> 00:43:53,240
Q. Can I try that question another way?

507
00:43:53,240 --> 00:43:57,240
I follow you when you say that we avoid the problem often

508
00:43:57,240 --> 00:43:58,240
of seeking an answer.

509
00:43:58,240 --> 00:43:59,240
K. That's right, sir.

510
00:43:59,240 --> 00:44:01,240
Q. That gets us away from the what is.

511
00:44:01,240 --> 00:44:03,240
K. That's right, sir.

512
00:44:03,240 --> 00:44:07,240
Q. And in your writings you said the answer is in the problem.

513
00:44:07,240 --> 00:44:09,240
K. That's right, sir.

514
00:44:09,240 --> 00:44:12,240
Now, I want to know how to look at that what is.

515
00:44:12,240 --> 00:44:17,240
Q. Okay. And how do I know the answer when I found the answer?

516
00:44:17,240 --> 00:44:18,240
What is the knowing process?

517
00:44:18,240 --> 00:44:21,240
Or do I only know what the answer was since thought is old?

518
00:44:21,240 --> 00:44:23,240
K. That's part of my question.

519
00:44:23,240 --> 00:44:24,240
What is the question, sir?

520
00:44:24,240 --> 00:44:27,240
Q. If I know the answer, if I focus on an attention,

521
00:44:27,240 --> 00:44:29,240
my attention on a problem,

522
00:44:29,240 --> 00:44:32,240
whether it's violence or loneliness or whatever,

523
00:44:32,240 --> 00:44:36,240
how is it if I really pay attention to the problem,

524
00:44:36,240 --> 00:44:38,240
to say, that's the answer,

525
00:44:38,240 --> 00:44:40,240
or am I thinking then and thought is old?

526
00:44:40,240 --> 00:44:43,240
K. Then there is no problem, sir.

527
00:44:45,240 --> 00:44:48,240
No, no, no, please, please, please, do...

528
00:44:48,240 --> 00:44:51,240
Please don't waste your energy clapping.

529
00:44:51,240 --> 00:44:53,240
It's not worth it.

530
00:44:54,240 --> 00:44:58,240
No, please, sir, do listen to this.

531
00:44:59,240 --> 00:45:04,240
You see, we are looking at life,

532
00:45:04,240 --> 00:45:06,240
living and everything with the eyes

533
00:45:06,240 --> 00:45:10,240
that have been so burdened with the past

534
00:45:10,240 --> 00:45:14,240
that our eyes never see anything new.

535
00:45:15,240 --> 00:45:20,240
Now, we are trying to find out

536
00:45:20,240 --> 00:45:26,240
what the transcending of violence is.

537
00:45:26,240 --> 00:45:31,240
I am saying, don't escape from it first,

538
00:45:32,240 --> 00:45:34,240
verbally or non-verbally,

539
00:45:34,240 --> 00:45:40,240
don't move away from that central fact of violence.

540
00:45:41,240 --> 00:45:44,240
Then the next question is,

541
00:45:44,240 --> 00:45:49,240
how do you know it is violence?

542
00:45:50,240 --> 00:45:55,240
You understand?

543
00:45:55,240 --> 00:46:00,240
You only know it because you are able to recognise it

544
00:46:00,240 --> 00:46:04,240
because you have been violent.

545
00:46:04,240 --> 00:46:08,240
But when you look at it without naming,

546
00:46:08,240 --> 00:46:11,240
without justifying, condemning,

547
00:46:11,240 --> 00:46:14,240
which are all the conditioning of the past,

548
00:46:14,240 --> 00:46:20,240
then you are looking at it with fresh eyes, aren't you?

549
00:46:20,240 --> 00:46:23,240
Then is it violence?

550
00:46:23,240 --> 00:46:25,240
Oh, no, don't say, no, sir,

551
00:46:25,240 --> 00:46:30,240
this is one of the most difficult things to do,

552
00:46:30,240 --> 00:46:35,240
because all our living is the past.

553
00:46:36,240 --> 00:46:41,240
Do you know what it is to live in the present?

554
00:46:41,240 --> 00:46:45,240
Q. Why is it important?

555
00:46:45,240 --> 00:46:49,240
K. Why is it important?

556
00:46:49,240 --> 00:46:52,240
Why do you ask that question, why is it important?

557
00:46:52,240 --> 00:46:54,240
Q. Why are we trying to understand

558
00:46:54,240 --> 00:46:56,240
why do we want to lead a life of love?

559
00:46:56,240 --> 00:47:01,240
K. Why do you want to lead a life of love?

560
00:47:01,240 --> 00:47:05,240
I don't.

561
00:47:05,240 --> 00:47:09,240
I want to lead – not even I don't want to –

562
00:47:09,240 --> 00:47:14,240
I see violence and I see the misery it brings about

563
00:47:14,240 --> 00:47:21,240
to the mother, to the man, to human beings,

564
00:47:21,240 --> 00:47:27,240
and I ask myself, as a human being, can this end?

565
00:47:27,240 --> 00:47:32,240
And in enquiring into the question of ending,

566
00:47:32,240 --> 00:47:36,240
I find out what it is to live peacefully, that's all.

567
00:47:36,240 --> 00:47:43,240
Not that I want to end, which is another form of action of will.

568
00:47:44,240 --> 00:47:50,240
Sir, look, therefore, then the next question is,

569
00:47:50,240 --> 00:47:57,240
the mind is the result of the past.

570
00:47:57,240 --> 00:48:00,240
Right?

571
00:48:00,240 --> 00:48:05,240
The mind recognises violence, names it,

572
00:48:05,240 --> 00:48:09,240
and it moves away from it.

573
00:48:09,240 --> 00:48:13,240
Now, when the mind doesn't name it,

574
00:48:13,240 --> 00:48:20,240
can the mind look at what it has called violence?

575
00:48:22,240 --> 00:48:27,240
Then is there such a thing as violence?

576
00:48:27,240 --> 00:48:34,240
And to look, your mind must be extraordinarily free of the past.

577
00:48:34,240 --> 00:48:38,240
Right?

578
00:48:38,240 --> 00:48:42,240
To look at my wife or my husband,

579
00:48:42,240 --> 00:48:47,240
the mind must be free of the image that it has built,

580
00:48:47,240 --> 00:48:51,240
the image being the past.

581
00:48:51,240 --> 00:48:55,240
To understand that,

582
00:48:55,240 --> 00:49:00,240
and to be aware at the moment of the insult or the flattery,

583
00:49:00,240 --> 00:49:04,240
to be aware at that moment.

584
00:49:05,240 --> 00:49:08,240
If the mind is not aware,

585
00:49:08,240 --> 00:49:14,240
it has already become inattentive and therefore building an image.

586
00:49:14,240 --> 00:49:18,240
This is clear, is it?

587
00:49:18,240 --> 00:49:21,240
Are you doing this?

588
00:49:21,240 --> 00:49:25,240
Q. You say free, be free of it, that includes a lot more.

589
00:49:25,240 --> 00:49:27,240
How far does that go?

590
00:49:27,240 --> 00:49:32,240
Q. Would you mind freedom, would you go into that?

591
00:49:33,240 --> 00:49:37,240
K. Would you go into freedom? What does it mean?

592
00:49:37,240 --> 00:49:41,240
We'll come to that, sir, presently.

593
00:49:41,240 --> 00:49:48,240
So, there are all the deep down

594
00:49:49,240 --> 00:49:54,240
angers, frustrations, resistances.

595
00:49:54,240 --> 00:49:59,240
The mind must also be free of that, mustn't it?

596
00:49:59,240 --> 00:50:05,240
The mind can be free of active violence in the present.

597
00:50:05,240 --> 00:50:08,240
Right?

598
00:50:08,240 --> 00:50:09,240
Are you following this?

599
00:50:09,240 --> 00:50:14,240
I am asking, can the mind be free

600
00:50:14,240 --> 00:50:19,240
of all the unconscious accumulations

601
00:50:19,240 --> 00:50:24,240
of hate, anger, bitterness,

602
00:50:25,240 --> 00:50:29,240
which are there deep down?

603
00:50:29,240 --> 00:50:33,240
You follow? How is this to be done?

604
00:50:33,240 --> 00:50:36,240
Q. Why is this to be done?

605
00:50:36,240 --> 00:50:39,240
K. The gentleman says, why should it be done?

606
00:50:39,240 --> 00:50:41,240
Q. Why not? Well, why not, too?

607
00:50:41,240 --> 00:50:45,240
K. Oh, no, come off it.

608
00:50:49,240 --> 00:50:52,240
Why should it be done and why not?

609
00:50:52,240 --> 00:50:55,240
Then we end up in – you know.

610
00:50:55,240 --> 00:50:57,240
It should be done because, sir,

611
00:50:57,240 --> 00:51:00,240
a man who wants to live at peace

612
00:51:00,240 --> 00:51:03,240
and to bring about a world that is peaceful

613
00:51:03,240 --> 00:51:07,240
must enquire into all this,

614
00:51:07,240 --> 00:51:13,240
must, as a human being, see if he can be free from it.

615
00:51:13,240 --> 00:51:16,240
And that's what we are trying to do.

616
00:51:16,240 --> 00:51:19,240
Q. But if one sees his violence in oneself

617
00:51:19,240 --> 00:51:21,240
and outside of oneself,

618
00:51:21,240 --> 00:51:25,240
how does one keep from being depressed or disturbed by it?

619
00:51:25,240 --> 00:51:26,240
K. Excuse me?

620
00:51:26,240 --> 00:51:33,240
Q. How does one keep from being depressed or disturbed by it?

621
00:51:33,240 --> 00:51:38,240
K. How does one keep from being depressed or disturbed by it?

622
00:51:38,240 --> 00:51:45,240
K. How do – if one is clear and is free of this violence,

623
00:51:45,240 --> 00:51:51,240
you are asking, how can one be free of depression?

624
00:51:51,240 --> 00:51:53,240
Q. No, one sees the violence.

625
00:51:53,240 --> 00:51:55,240
K. About you.

626
00:51:55,240 --> 00:51:57,240
Ah, I see.

627
00:51:57,240 --> 00:52:02,240
If one is free of this violence in oneself,

628
00:52:02,240 --> 00:52:05,240
and when you see violence outside of you,

629
00:52:05,240 --> 00:52:08,240
doesn't it depress you?

630
00:52:08,240 --> 00:52:11,240
What are you to do?

631
00:52:11,240 --> 00:52:13,240
Is that it?

632
00:52:13,240 --> 00:52:18,240
What are you to do is to teach another.

633
00:52:22,240 --> 00:52:28,240
Sir, teaching another is the highest profession in the world,

634
00:52:28,240 --> 00:52:32,240
not for money,

635
00:52:33,240 --> 00:52:36,240
not for your big bank account,

636
00:52:36,240 --> 00:52:38,240
just to teach, to tell another,

637
00:52:38,240 --> 00:52:43,240
tell another, look, you can live differently, for God's sake, look.

638
00:52:43,240 --> 00:52:45,240
Q. What is the easiest way to teach that?

639
00:52:45,240 --> 00:52:50,240
K. What is the easiest way? Go to college.

640
00:52:56,240 --> 00:53:01,240
No, no, no, this is becoming a circus.

641
00:53:01,240 --> 00:53:06,240
Sir, you teach another

642
00:53:06,240 --> 00:53:13,240
by teaching him and therefore learning yourself.

643
00:53:13,240 --> 00:53:18,240
In teaching him, you are learning.

644
00:53:18,240 --> 00:53:19,240
You understand?

645
00:53:19,240 --> 00:53:23,240
First you have learnt, accumulated knowledge,

646
00:53:23,240 --> 00:53:25,240
then you inform,

647
00:53:25,240 --> 00:53:29,240
whereas you are not learning.

648
00:53:29,240 --> 00:53:35,240
You inform, whereas you yourself are violent,

649
00:53:35,240 --> 00:53:41,240
understanding yourself is to help another to understand it.

650
00:53:41,240 --> 00:53:47,240
And therefore the teaching is the learning.

651
00:53:48,240 --> 00:53:51,240
Sir, you don't see all the beauty of all this.

652
00:53:51,240 --> 00:53:54,240
Too bad.

653
00:53:54,240 --> 00:53:58,240
So let's go on.

654
00:53:58,240 --> 00:54:09,240
Sir, I mean, don't you want to know from your heart what love is?

655
00:54:10,240 --> 00:54:14,240
Don't you? No?

656
00:54:14,240 --> 00:54:17,240
He doesn't know.

657
00:54:18,240 --> 00:54:23,240
Isn't it a human cry, which has been for millennia,

658
00:54:23,240 --> 00:54:26,240
to find out how to live peacefully,

659
00:54:26,240 --> 00:54:31,240
how to have real abundance, compassion?

660
00:54:31,240 --> 00:54:36,240
And that can only come into being when there is no violence,

661
00:54:36,240 --> 00:54:44,240
when there is real sense of non-me.

662
00:54:44,240 --> 00:54:46,240
You understand?

663
00:54:46,240 --> 00:54:52,240
And that's what we are enquiring into.

664
00:54:52,240 --> 00:54:59,240
And we say, look, to find that out, don't escape,

665
00:55:00,240 --> 00:55:02,240
whether it is loneliness, whether it is anger,

666
00:55:02,240 --> 00:55:08,240
whether it is bitterness, look at it without any escape.

667
00:55:08,240 --> 00:55:13,240
The escape is the naming of it also.

668
00:55:13,240 --> 00:55:17,240
So when you are bitter, don't name it, look at it.

669
00:55:17,240 --> 00:55:23,240
And then, see, if you don't name, does bitterness exist?

670
00:55:23,240 --> 00:55:26,240
You understand? Yes, sir?

671
00:55:26,240 --> 00:55:30,240
Q. Why is the animal, which apparently has no name but not me,

672
00:55:30,240 --> 00:55:33,240
why is it violent?

673
00:55:33,240 --> 00:55:39,240
K. Why is the animal, which apparently doesn't name,

674
00:55:39,240 --> 00:55:42,240
why is it violent?

675
00:55:42,240 --> 00:55:44,240
Is the animal asking the question

676
00:55:44,240 --> 00:55:48,240
or the human being asking the question?

677
00:55:49,240 --> 00:55:53,240
I am not being insulting, sir, but I am asking.

678
00:55:53,240 --> 00:55:57,240
The animal is hungry.

679
00:55:57,240 --> 00:56:03,240
We are supposed to be intelligent and attack the animal

680
00:56:03,240 --> 00:56:09,240
to eat it, for sport and all the rest of the ugly business.

681
00:56:09,240 --> 00:56:15,240
With our violent eyes, we look at the animal.

682
00:56:16,240 --> 00:56:21,240
So, sir, please, let's stick to... Yes, madame?

683
00:56:21,240 --> 00:56:24,240
Q. Excuse me. I'd like to ask two questions.

684
00:56:24,240 --> 00:56:27,240
We've established there's violence in all of our lives,

685
00:56:27,240 --> 00:56:31,240
but what I'm waiting for is how do we get rid of this violence?

686
00:56:31,240 --> 00:56:35,240
I'm showing it to you, madame.

687
00:56:36,240 --> 00:56:39,240
I'm showing it to you.

688
00:56:39,240 --> 00:56:41,240
Q. I'm missing the point that I'm afraid.

689
00:56:41,240 --> 00:56:44,240
You mean merely by facing the fact that there is violence.

690
00:56:44,240 --> 00:56:49,240
No, madame, it's much more complex than that.

691
00:56:50,240 --> 00:56:52,240
Q. And one more question.

692
00:56:52,240 --> 00:56:54,240
Do you advocate getting rid of all violence

693
00:56:54,240 --> 00:56:59,240
or is some violence healthy in everyone's life?

694
00:56:59,240 --> 00:57:01,240
Q. I don't mean physical violence.

695
00:57:01,240 --> 00:57:03,240
I mean getting rid of frustrations.

696
00:57:03,240 --> 00:57:05,240
Can this be helpful?

697
00:57:05,240 --> 00:57:09,240
Or are you trying to keep you from being frustrated?

698
00:57:09,240 --> 00:57:14,240
K. No, madame. Look, answer the second question.

699
00:57:15,240 --> 00:57:19,240
Why are we frustrated?

700
00:57:19,240 --> 00:57:24,240
Have you ever asked yourself why you are frustrated?

701
00:57:24,240 --> 00:57:29,240
To answer that question, have you ever asked what is fulfilment?

702
00:57:29,240 --> 00:57:33,240
Why you want to fulfil?

703
00:57:34,240 --> 00:57:39,240
And is there such a thing as fulfilment?

704
00:57:46,240 --> 00:57:48,240
Please, answer it.

705
00:57:48,240 --> 00:57:51,240
This is a discreet question.

706
00:57:51,240 --> 00:57:56,240
Please, answer it. This is a discussion.

707
00:57:57,240 --> 00:58:00,240
Is there such a thing as fulfilment?

708
00:58:00,240 --> 00:58:03,240
What is it that is fulfilling?

709
00:58:03,240 --> 00:58:06,240
The me?

710
00:58:06,240 --> 00:58:09,240
The me that is violent?

711
00:58:09,240 --> 00:58:12,240
The me that is separating?

712
00:58:12,240 --> 00:58:16,240
The me that says, I'm bigger than you?

713
00:58:16,240 --> 00:58:20,240
The me that pursues ambition, fame, notoriety,

714
00:58:20,240 --> 00:58:24,240
what it will, and because it wants to achieve,

715
00:58:24,240 --> 00:58:28,240
therefore it's frustrated when it cannot achieve,

716
00:58:28,240 --> 00:58:30,240
and therefore becomes bitter,

717
00:58:30,240 --> 00:58:35,240
therefore is there such a thing as fulfilment?

718
00:58:35,240 --> 00:58:42,240
Or only the me wanting to expand itself,

719
00:58:42,240 --> 00:58:46,240
and when it cannot expand it feels frustrated,

720
00:58:46,240 --> 00:58:49,240
and therefore bitter.

721
00:58:49,240 --> 00:58:55,240
And that bitterness, that desire to expand is violence.

722
00:58:58,240 --> 00:59:04,240
Now, when you see that, the truth of that,

723
00:59:04,240 --> 00:59:07,240
then there is no fulfilment at all,

724
00:59:07,240 --> 00:59:12,240
therefore there is no frustration. Oh, Lord!

725
00:59:15,240 --> 00:59:16,240
Yes, sir?

726
00:59:16,240 --> 00:59:19,240
Plants and animals are both living things,

727
00:59:19,240 --> 00:59:21,240
they both try to survive.

728
00:59:21,240 --> 00:59:27,240
Do you draw a distinction between killing animals to eat

729
00:59:27,240 --> 00:59:31,240
and killing plants to eat, if so, why?

730
00:59:33,240 --> 00:59:39,240
Personally, I have never eaten meat in all my life.

731
00:59:39,240 --> 00:59:44,240
One has to survive, I don't know why,

732
00:59:44,240 --> 00:59:51,240
so one needs, kills the least thing that is a vegetable.

733
00:59:51,240 --> 00:59:53,240
Right?

734
00:59:55,240 --> 00:59:58,240
And I believe some scientists are gradually coming

735
00:59:58,240 --> 01:00:01,240
to that point of view also.

736
01:00:01,240 --> 01:00:04,240
Then you'll all accept it.

737
01:00:04,240 --> 01:00:08,240
It seems to me the part of the past is the mental pattern of thinking.

738
01:00:08,240 --> 01:00:11,240
And all these questions are Aristotelian thinking,

739
01:00:11,240 --> 01:00:14,240
and you are using non-Aristotelian thinking,

740
01:00:14,240 --> 01:00:16,240
and that seems to be why there is such a gap.

741
01:00:16,240 --> 01:00:19,240
In other words, to look at something is to use a non-Aristotelian...

742
01:00:19,240 --> 01:00:20,240
That's right, sir.

743
01:00:20,240 --> 01:00:23,240
Well, then everyone here is talking Aristotelian thinking,

744
01:00:23,240 --> 01:00:26,240
and you are using a non-Aristotelian thinking.

745
01:00:26,240 --> 01:00:29,240
And that is the reason why there is such a gap.

746
01:00:30,240 --> 01:00:31,240
That's right, sir.

747
01:00:31,240 --> 01:00:33,240
Well, then everyone here is talking Aristotelian

748
01:00:33,240 --> 01:00:35,240
and thinking Aristotelian,

749
01:00:35,240 --> 01:00:37,240
and you are using non-Aristotelian tactics,

750
01:00:37,240 --> 01:00:40,240
and therefore the gap is so complete, I'm amazed.

751
01:00:40,240 --> 01:00:42,240
And I suggest that we all get non-Aristotelian

752
01:00:42,240 --> 01:00:44,240
and then we can commune very closely.

753
01:00:44,240 --> 01:00:47,240
That is the difficulty, sir. I know this.

754
01:00:49,240 --> 01:00:52,240
Just a minute, sir, one moment.

755
01:00:52,240 --> 01:00:55,240
Just a minute, sir, please look at it.

756
01:00:56,240 --> 01:01:00,240
What that gentleman said was,

757
01:01:01,240 --> 01:01:06,240
you are used to one particular formula,

758
01:01:06,240 --> 01:01:10,240
particular series of languages with a certain meaning,

759
01:01:10,240 --> 01:01:18,240
and the speaker has not that particular view.

760
01:01:18,240 --> 01:01:22,240
So the difficulty lies in communication.

761
01:01:22,240 --> 01:01:24,240
And we went into that.

762
01:01:24,240 --> 01:01:28,240
He said the word is not the thing,

763
01:01:28,240 --> 01:01:32,240
the description is not the described,

764
01:01:32,240 --> 01:01:36,240
the explanation is not the explained,

765
01:01:36,240 --> 01:01:40,240
and you keep on sticking to the explanation,

766
01:01:40,240 --> 01:01:43,240
holding on to the word,

767
01:01:43,240 --> 01:01:47,240
and that's why our difficulty is.

768
01:01:55,240 --> 01:02:00,240
We see what violence is in the world.

769
01:02:00,240 --> 01:02:03,240
It's part of fear, part of pleasure,

770
01:02:03,240 --> 01:02:10,240
part of this tremendous drive for excitement.

771
01:02:12,240 --> 01:02:16,240
And we want that,

772
01:02:16,240 --> 01:02:23,240
and therefore we encourage society to give that to us.

773
01:02:24,240 --> 01:02:28,240
And we blame the society,

774
01:02:29,240 --> 01:02:34,240
whereas we are responsible for all this.

775
01:02:34,240 --> 01:02:38,240
And we are saying, asking ourselves,

776
01:02:38,240 --> 01:02:44,240
whether this violence which is such terrific energy,

777
01:02:44,240 --> 01:02:48,240
can that energy be used differently?

778
01:02:48,240 --> 01:02:51,240
Right?

779
01:02:51,240 --> 01:02:56,240
To be violent needs energy.

780
01:02:58,240 --> 01:03:03,240
Now, can that energy be transformed

781
01:03:03,240 --> 01:03:06,240
or moved in another direction?

782
01:03:06,240 --> 01:03:10,240
We are putting the same thing differently.

783
01:03:14,240 --> 01:03:20,240
Now, look, any form of resistance is a waste of energy.

784
01:03:20,240 --> 01:03:23,240
Right?

785
01:03:24,240 --> 01:03:28,240
Because that breeds violence.

786
01:03:29,240 --> 01:03:35,240
Resisting one nation against another nation,

787
01:03:35,240 --> 01:03:39,240
one nation saying, I am better than you,

788
01:03:39,240 --> 01:03:42,240
and so on, resisting.

789
01:03:42,240 --> 01:03:45,240
The resistance between wife and husband,

790
01:03:45,240 --> 01:03:48,240
resistance, you understand,

791
01:03:48,240 --> 01:03:56,240
is energy which breeds division and therefore violence.

792
01:03:56,240 --> 01:04:01,240
Now, understanding that, seeing the truth of that,

793
01:04:01,240 --> 01:04:06,240
that energy now becomes entirely different, doesn't it?

794
01:04:06,240 --> 01:04:09,240
No?

795
01:04:09,240 --> 01:04:12,240
Mark, K.

796
01:04:12,240 --> 01:04:17,240
Q. How can a person observe the balance between

797
01:04:17,240 --> 01:04:21,240
the power of the mind and the existence of the person?

798
01:04:21,240 --> 01:04:23,240
K. All right, that's a good question.

799
01:04:23,240 --> 01:04:29,240
How can one observe the total process,

800
01:04:29,240 --> 01:04:31,240
the totality of anything,

801
01:04:31,240 --> 01:04:39,240
without the division, without resistance?

802
01:04:39,240 --> 01:04:42,240
Right?

803
01:04:45,240 --> 01:04:51,240
Have you ever observed totally anything?

804
01:04:52,240 --> 01:04:56,240
Anything, it doesn't matter what.

805
01:04:56,240 --> 01:05:04,240
An ant moving across the floor, have you watched it totally?

806
01:05:04,240 --> 01:05:10,240
Or do you step on it, or throw it out?

807
01:05:10,240 --> 01:05:15,240
Have you watched it very, very closely?

808
01:05:15,240 --> 01:05:19,240
I am afraid you haven't.

809
01:05:20,240 --> 01:05:24,240
Have you ever watched a tree totally?

810
01:05:24,240 --> 01:05:27,240
Which means not saying how beautiful it is,

811
01:05:27,240 --> 01:05:31,240
or how ugly it is, or I wish I had it in my garden.

812
01:05:31,240 --> 01:05:35,240
Have you ever watched it totally?

813
01:05:35,240 --> 01:05:39,240
Have you ever watched the cloud with the light on it,

814
01:05:39,240 --> 01:05:42,240
marvellous sight, completely?

815
01:05:42,240 --> 01:05:47,240
Or you say, this lovely cloud, let's go and have tea.

816
01:05:48,240 --> 01:05:50,240
No, sir, do look at it.

817
01:05:50,240 --> 01:05:54,240
Have you ever watched your wife totally, or husband?

818
01:05:54,240 --> 01:05:57,240
No, sir.

819
01:05:57,240 --> 01:06:03,240
And therefore if you watch totally there is no resistance.

820
01:06:03,240 --> 01:06:08,240
It is this inattention that breeds resistance.

821
01:06:08,240 --> 01:06:11,240
Oh, come on, sir.

822
01:06:11,240 --> 01:06:14,240
Q. When you look at another person totally,

823
01:06:14,240 --> 01:06:17,240
doesn't it seem to make them uncomfortable?

824
01:06:17,240 --> 01:06:21,240
K. Ah, when you watch a person totally,

825
01:06:21,240 --> 01:06:25,240
you make the other person rather uncomfortable.

826
01:06:25,240 --> 01:06:28,240
I am afraid you do,

827
01:06:28,240 --> 01:06:33,240
because they don't want you to look at him totally.

828
01:06:33,240 --> 01:06:37,240
But you can do it casually.

829
01:06:49,240 --> 01:06:52,240
So, please, sir, come back.

830
01:06:53,240 --> 01:06:56,240
What we are discussing is really quite serious,

831
01:06:56,240 --> 01:06:59,240
I wish you would pay attention to it.

832
01:06:59,240 --> 01:07:01,240
You want to be entertained, I am afraid,

833
01:07:01,240 --> 01:07:06,240
I am not the kind of person who wants to entertain.

834
01:07:07,240 --> 01:07:14,240
Q. Sir, non-violence that is absolute is another thing.

835
01:07:14,240 --> 01:07:19,240
Violence itself is an aberration of what it could be.

836
01:07:20,240 --> 01:07:24,240
K. Yes, if you want to put it that way.

837
01:07:25,240 --> 01:07:29,240
Sir, look, what we are saying is,

838
01:07:29,240 --> 01:07:33,240
violence is a form of energy.

839
01:07:39,240 --> 01:07:43,240
And love is also a form of energy.

840
01:07:43,240 --> 01:07:48,240
Love without jealousy, without anxiety, without fear,

841
01:07:48,240 --> 01:07:55,240
without bitterness, without all the agony that goes with love.

842
01:07:58,240 --> 01:08:02,240
Now, violence is energy,

843
01:08:02,240 --> 01:08:08,240
love hedged about, surrounded, contained with jealousy,

844
01:08:08,240 --> 01:08:12,240
all that, is another form of energy.

845
01:08:12,240 --> 01:08:17,240
Now, to transcend both, go beyond both,

846
01:08:17,240 --> 01:08:20,240
is also another energy.

847
01:08:20,240 --> 01:08:24,240
It is the same energy moving totally in a different direction

848
01:08:24,240 --> 01:08:28,240
and dimension. Right?

849
01:08:28,240 --> 01:08:31,240
Q. But wouldn't both of those energies be the same?

850
01:08:31,240 --> 01:08:36,240
K. We are saying that, sir. No, we are saying, look, sir.

851
01:08:36,240 --> 01:08:40,240
Non-Aristotelian language.

852
01:08:40,240 --> 01:08:45,240
Q. No, I am saying, is love with jealousy, is actually violence?

853
01:08:45,240 --> 01:08:47,240
K. Of course it is.

854
01:08:47,240 --> 01:08:50,240
Q. So in other words, you have two energies and you have the violence.

855
01:08:50,240 --> 01:08:53,240
K. It is the same energy, sir.

856
01:08:53,240 --> 01:08:56,240
Madame, let's say more...

857
01:08:56,240 --> 01:09:04,240
Q. At what stage and under what conditions is a certain individual

858
01:09:04,240 --> 01:09:08,240
to go into psychic practices and experiences,

859
01:09:08,240 --> 01:09:13,240
and to what extent? Please.

860
01:09:16,240 --> 01:09:20,240
K. What are you saying, madame?

861
01:09:20,240 --> 01:09:23,240
Q. When should we have psychic experience?

862
01:09:23,240 --> 01:09:29,240
K. When should we have psychic experience?

863
01:09:29,240 --> 01:09:33,240
What has that to do with violence?

864
01:09:33,240 --> 01:09:36,240
Do, please, just listen.

865
01:09:36,240 --> 01:09:41,240
When should you have psychic experience?

866
01:09:44,240 --> 01:09:48,240
Never.

867
01:09:50,240 --> 01:09:54,240
Do you know what it means to have psychic experiences?

868
01:09:55,240 --> 01:10:00,240
Do you know what it means to have psychic experiences?

869
01:10:00,240 --> 01:10:08,240
To have the experience, extra-sensory, perceptive experience,

870
01:10:08,240 --> 01:10:13,240
you must be extraordinarily mature,

871
01:10:14,240 --> 01:10:17,240
you must be extraordinarily sensitive,

872
01:10:17,240 --> 01:10:21,240
and therefore extraordinarily intelligent.

873
01:10:21,240 --> 01:10:24,240
And if you are extraordinarily intelligent,

874
01:10:24,240 --> 01:10:28,240
you don't want psychic experiences.

875
01:10:34,240 --> 01:10:37,240
Sirs, do look.

876
01:10:37,240 --> 01:10:41,240
Give your heart to this, please,

877
01:10:41,240 --> 01:10:48,240
because human beings are destroying each other through violence.

878
01:10:48,240 --> 01:10:50,240
The husband is destroying the wife,

879
01:10:50,240 --> 01:10:53,240
and the wife is destroying the husband,

880
01:10:53,240 --> 01:10:57,240
though they sleep together, walk together.

881
01:11:00,240 --> 01:11:04,240
Each lives in isolation,

882
01:11:04,240 --> 01:11:08,240
with his own problems, with his own anxieties,

883
01:11:08,240 --> 01:11:12,240
and this isolation is violence.

884
01:11:13,240 --> 01:11:17,240
Now, when you see all this so clearly in front of you,

885
01:11:17,240 --> 01:11:21,240
see it, not just think about it.

886
01:11:22,240 --> 01:11:27,240
When you see the danger of it, you act, don't you?

887
01:11:27,240 --> 01:11:33,240
Look, when you see a dangerous animal, you act, don't you?

888
01:11:33,240 --> 01:11:35,240
There is no hesitation,

889
01:11:35,240 --> 01:11:39,240
there is no argument between you and the animal.

890
01:11:39,240 --> 01:11:44,240
You just act, you run away or do something.

891
01:11:44,240 --> 01:11:48,240
Here we are arguing.

892
01:11:48,240 --> 01:11:53,240
You don't see the tremendous danger of violence.

893
01:11:53,240 --> 01:11:58,240
You only see the end result of violence, which is the bomb.

894
01:12:03,240 --> 01:12:06,240
So if you actually, with your heart,

895
01:12:06,240 --> 01:12:11,240
see the nature of violence and see the danger of it,

896
01:12:11,240 --> 01:12:15,240
you are finished with it.

897
01:12:16,240 --> 01:12:21,240
But you see, now how can one point out the danger of it

898
01:12:21,240 --> 01:12:25,240
if you don't want to see it?

899
01:12:25,240 --> 01:12:32,240
Either Aristotelian, non-Aristotelian language won't help you.

900
01:12:32,240 --> 01:12:35,240
Yes, sir?

901
01:12:35,240 --> 01:12:40,240
Q. There have been groups in India, here and other places

902
01:12:40,240 --> 01:12:44,240
where living in a society which is violent,

903
01:12:44,240 --> 01:12:49,240
they said, we will not be violent.

904
01:12:49,240 --> 01:12:52,240
K. Yes, sir.

905
01:12:52,240 --> 01:12:56,240
Q. There are groups in India, here and other places

906
01:12:56,240 --> 01:12:59,240
where living in a society which is violent,

907
01:12:59,240 --> 01:13:03,240
they said, we will not be violent.

908
01:13:03,240 --> 01:13:07,240
But we are going much further than that.

909
01:13:07,240 --> 01:13:11,240
They may not have violence against the community,

910
01:13:11,240 --> 01:13:16,240
but they are violent in themselves.

911
01:13:16,240 --> 01:13:19,240
You don't see the point.

912
01:13:19,240 --> 01:13:24,240
Q. Sir, I feel that I see what you are saying,

913
01:13:24,240 --> 01:13:28,240
and I have tried that, of watching violence in myself

914
01:13:28,240 --> 01:13:31,240
about naming.

915
01:13:31,240 --> 01:13:33,240
The gentleman who asked the first question

916
01:13:33,240 --> 01:13:36,240
about having been in a concentration camp,

917
01:13:36,240 --> 01:13:41,240
being a vegetarian, how do we meet violence?

918
01:13:41,240 --> 01:13:48,240
I feel like, how do we meet violence in other people?

919
01:13:48,240 --> 01:13:50,240
Do we do it in the same way?

920
01:13:50,240 --> 01:13:53,240
K. How do you meet violence in other people?

921
01:13:53,240 --> 01:13:58,240
That is really quite a difficult problem, isn't it?

922
01:14:00,240 --> 01:14:05,240
My neighbour is violent, violent towards me,

923
01:14:05,240 --> 01:14:10,240
how shall I deal with him?

924
01:14:10,240 --> 01:14:15,240
Turn the other cheek? He is delighted.

925
01:14:18,240 --> 01:14:21,240
What shall I do?

926
01:14:21,240 --> 01:14:25,240
If you ask that question – do please, I am asking this seriously –

927
01:14:25,240 --> 01:14:32,240
would you ask that question if there was no violence in you?

928
01:14:34,240 --> 01:14:38,240
No, do listen, sir, please do listen to this question.

929
01:14:38,240 --> 01:14:44,240
If in your heart, in your mind there is no violence at all,

930
01:14:44,240 --> 01:14:48,240
not a spot, no hate, no bitterness,

931
01:14:48,240 --> 01:14:52,240
no sense of fulfilment, no wanting to be famous,

932
01:14:52,240 --> 01:14:57,240
you know, no violence at all.

933
01:14:58,240 --> 01:15:02,240
Would you ask that question how you would meet the neighbour

934
01:15:02,240 --> 01:15:04,240
who is violent,

935
01:15:04,240 --> 01:15:10,240
or you would know then what to do with your neighbour?

936
01:15:10,240 --> 01:15:15,240
Others may call what you do violent,

937
01:15:15,240 --> 01:15:20,240
but you may not be violent. You follow?

938
01:15:20,240 --> 01:15:23,240
You have no violence.

939
01:15:23,240 --> 01:15:27,240
And at the moment your neighbour acts violently,

940
01:15:27,240 --> 01:15:31,240
you will know how to deal with it.

941
01:15:31,240 --> 01:15:34,240
But the third person watching you might say,

942
01:15:34,240 --> 01:15:38,240
by Jove, you are also violent.

943
01:15:38,240 --> 01:15:43,240
But you know you are not violent.

944
01:15:43,240 --> 01:15:48,240
So what is important is to be for yourself

945
01:15:48,240 --> 01:15:52,240
completely without violence.

946
01:15:52,240 --> 01:15:56,240
And it doesn't matter what another calls you.

947
01:15:56,240 --> 01:16:00,240
You know it, you know it, you know it.

948
01:16:00,240 --> 01:16:04,240
It doesn't matter what another calls you.

949
01:16:04,240 --> 01:16:08,240
You know in your heart you are not.

950
01:16:12,240 --> 01:16:18,240
Q. Isn't the belief in the unity of all things

951
01:16:18,240 --> 01:16:24,240
just as human as the belief in the division of all things?

952
01:16:24,240 --> 01:16:29,240
K. Belief in the unity of all human beings.

953
01:16:30,240 --> 01:16:34,240
No, sir, don't believe.

954
01:16:34,240 --> 01:16:40,240
Why do you want to believe in the unity of all human beings?

955
01:16:42,240 --> 01:16:47,240
We are not united, that is a fact.

956
01:16:47,240 --> 01:16:53,240
Why do you want to believe in something which is non-factual?

957
01:16:53,240 --> 01:16:57,240
Sir, that brings up the whole question of belief.

958
01:16:57,240 --> 01:16:59,240
You see, that is just it.

959
01:16:59,240 --> 01:17:04,240
You have your belief and another has his belief.

960
01:17:04,240 --> 01:17:09,240
And we are fighting, killing each other for belief.

961
01:17:09,240 --> 01:17:13,240
The communist has his belief, Stalin had his belief,

962
01:17:13,240 --> 01:17:17,240
and he destroyed millions.

963
01:17:18,240 --> 01:17:23,240
Now, why do you have any belief at all?

964
01:17:24,240 --> 01:17:28,240
You have belief because you are afraid.

965
01:17:30,240 --> 01:17:33,240
No?

966
01:17:33,240 --> 01:17:37,240
Do you believe that the sun rises?

967
01:17:37,240 --> 01:17:42,240
It is there to see it, you don't have to believe.

968
01:17:42,240 --> 01:17:47,240
So belief is a form of division,

969
01:17:47,240 --> 01:17:52,240
therefore belief is violence.

970
01:17:56,240 --> 01:18:04,240
So the mind, to be free of violence, implies all this,

971
01:18:04,240 --> 01:18:11,240
freedom from everything that man has put into another man.

972
01:18:12,240 --> 01:18:18,240
Belief, dogma, rituals, my country, your country,

973
01:18:18,240 --> 01:18:24,240
your god and my god, my opinion, your opinion, my ideal,

974
01:18:24,240 --> 01:18:29,240
all those help to divide human beings

975
01:18:29,240 --> 01:18:34,240
and therefore breed violence.

976
01:18:34,240 --> 01:18:38,240
And though religions have said, organised religions have said,

977
01:18:38,240 --> 01:18:43,240
have said, preached unity of mankind,

978
01:18:45,240 --> 01:18:49,240
each religion thinks it is far superior than the other,

979
01:18:49,240 --> 01:18:55,240
the Baptists against the – you know, you know it all very well.

980
01:18:57,240 --> 01:19:02,240
Q. Sir, who said unity of all things?

981
01:19:03,240 --> 01:19:07,240
K. Who said unity of all things?

982
01:19:07,240 --> 01:19:11,240
Sir, there is a unity of all things

983
01:19:11,240 --> 01:19:14,240
only when you know what love is.

984
01:19:14,240 --> 01:19:17,240
When there is love in your heart you will know it,

985
01:19:17,240 --> 01:19:19,240
don't talk about unity.

986
01:19:19,240 --> 01:19:24,240
When you are destroying your neighbour, don't talk about unity.

987
01:19:24,240 --> 01:19:29,240
Q. But sir, you have spoken now of freedom,

988
01:19:29,240 --> 01:19:32,240
you have spoken of freedom from.

989
01:19:32,240 --> 01:19:36,240
Can you tell us about freedom to?

990
01:19:36,240 --> 01:19:40,240
K. You have talked about freedom from.

991
01:19:40,240 --> 01:19:45,240
Will you say something about freedom to?

992
01:19:45,240 --> 01:19:50,240
Freedom from or freedom to is not freedom.

993
01:19:50,240 --> 01:19:55,240
Freedom is freedom, not from something towards something.

994
01:19:55,240 --> 01:19:58,240
Right?

995
01:19:58,240 --> 01:20:01,240
Q. I interpreted what you were talking about in unity

996
01:20:01,240 --> 01:20:05,240
that those who preach unity are actually aiding the division.

997
01:20:05,240 --> 01:20:08,240
K. Quite right, sir.

998
01:20:08,240 --> 01:20:11,240
Q. Is the actual understanding of this

999
01:20:11,240 --> 01:20:15,240
the relative scene and the effect that you actually understand?

1000
01:20:15,240 --> 01:20:18,240
K. Yes, sir.

1001
01:20:18,240 --> 01:20:23,240
Sir, look, when you see danger you do, you act.

1002
01:20:23,240 --> 01:20:29,240
If you see the danger of violence, see it, you then act,

1003
01:20:29,240 --> 01:20:32,240
but you don't see the danger of violence

1004
01:20:32,240 --> 01:20:35,240
because you are used to it, like belief.

1005
01:20:35,240 --> 01:20:39,240
You say, yes, why shouldn't I believe?

1006
01:20:39,240 --> 01:20:42,240
My opinion is as good as yours,

1007
01:20:43,240 --> 01:20:47,240
my opinion is as good as your opinion.

1008
01:20:47,240 --> 01:20:54,240
So, any divisive, dividing element in human beings

1009
01:20:54,240 --> 01:20:58,240
is productive of violence.

1010
01:20:58,240 --> 01:21:03,240
If one realises, understands that,

1011
01:21:03,240 --> 01:21:10,240
and then one watches – belief, will, desire to fulfil, to become,

1012
01:21:10,240 --> 01:21:16,240
you follow? – all these are breed violence,

1013
01:21:16,240 --> 01:21:18,240
which doesn't mean at the end of it

1014
01:21:18,240 --> 01:21:22,240
you live a vegetable kind of life.

1015
01:21:22,240 --> 01:21:29,240
On the contrary, you live in a totally different dimension,

1016
01:21:29,240 --> 01:21:34,240
which we'll talk about tomorrow when we talk about meditation.

1017
01:21:34,240 --> 01:21:39,240
Q. Sir, you've established that elimination of violence

1018
01:21:39,240 --> 01:21:43,240
will make it possible for everyone to be able to cope

1019
01:21:43,240 --> 01:21:45,240
with the material existence much easier.

1020
01:21:45,240 --> 01:21:49,240
In other words, to be able to completely eliminate the ego self.

1021
01:21:49,240 --> 01:21:53,240
Well, that's all very fine and it's very good,

1022
01:21:53,240 --> 01:21:56,240
but are you saying that this is the purpose for human life,

1023
01:21:56,240 --> 01:21:59,240
this is our purpose for living,

1024
01:21:59,240 --> 01:22:03,240
is just to be able to cope with the material existence?

1025
01:22:03,240 --> 01:22:10,240
Partly, sir, but also when you say,

1026
01:22:10,240 --> 01:22:14,240
is this the purpose of living?

1027
01:22:15,240 --> 01:22:19,240
Why do you want a purpose for living?

1028
01:22:19,240 --> 01:22:24,240
Living is its own purpose.

1029
01:22:24,240 --> 01:22:27,240
Why do you want a purpose?

1030
01:22:27,240 --> 01:22:33,240
You see, again, look at it. Look, sir, what we have done.

1031
01:22:33,240 --> 01:22:39,240
Each one has his own purpose. Right?

1032
01:22:39,240 --> 01:22:44,240
The religious man, his purpose, the scientist, his purpose,

1033
01:22:44,240 --> 01:22:50,240
the family, its purpose, and so on, divide it.

1034
01:22:50,240 --> 01:22:57,240
So, the life of a man who has a purpose is breeding violence,

1035
01:22:57,240 --> 01:23:00,240
because they divide.

1036
01:23:00,240 --> 01:23:06,240
Sir, it's all so clear and simple when you see the fact.

1037
01:23:06,240 --> 01:23:11,240
Q. Sir, you've employed the tool of reason and logic up to this point,

1038
01:23:11,240 --> 01:23:13,240
and probably throughout your entire lifetime,

1039
01:23:13,240 --> 01:23:16,240
to answer the questions that have come up in your mind.

1040
01:23:16,240 --> 01:23:19,240
Have you never reached a point to where you have found

1041
01:23:19,240 --> 01:23:23,240
a definite limitation to reason and logic?

1042
01:23:23,240 --> 01:23:27,240
K. Sir, I hope I'm not logical.

1043
01:23:27,240 --> 01:23:32,240
Logic must go to a certain extent.

1044
01:23:32,240 --> 01:23:39,240
One must think logically, sanely, healthily, up to a point, reason.

1045
01:23:39,240 --> 01:23:44,240
But after that, beyond that, there is much more.

1046
01:23:44,240 --> 01:23:47,240
Q. And you're saying that there is such a thing as an intuitional life.

1047
01:23:47,240 --> 01:23:49,240
K. Ah, wait a minute.

1048
01:23:49,240 --> 01:23:54,240
Now, when you use the word intuition, that's a dangerous word.

1049
01:23:57,240 --> 01:24:02,240
Intuition may be your own desire, your own wish,

1050
01:24:02,240 --> 01:24:07,240
saying, and you can say, that's my intuition.

1051
01:24:07,240 --> 01:24:13,240
What we are talking about is living a life in this world,

1052
01:24:13,240 --> 01:24:20,240
not escaping from this world, a life of non-violence,

1053
01:24:20,240 --> 01:24:26,240
a life, a really truly religious life,

1054
01:24:26,240 --> 01:24:30,240
not an intuitive life,

1055
01:24:31,240 --> 01:24:37,240
a life in which there is no conflict,

1056
01:24:37,240 --> 01:24:42,240
and a mind that's completely silent.

1057
01:24:42,240 --> 01:24:46,240
Again, we'll go into that when we talk about meditation.

1058
01:24:46,240 --> 01:24:50,240
Q. You said that life should be complete order,

1059
01:24:50,240 --> 01:24:54,240
and that complete order is precise in mathematics.

1060
01:24:54,240 --> 01:24:58,240
Therefore, wouldn't life in complete order be logical,

1061
01:24:58,240 --> 01:25:01,240
because mathematics is logical?

1062
01:25:01,240 --> 01:25:05,240
K. Sir, sir, when I said mathematical, I said in the sense,

1063
01:25:05,240 --> 01:25:12,240
you know, the highest form of mathematics is surely order.

1064
01:25:16,240 --> 01:25:19,240
Only in that sense. Yes, madame?

1065
01:25:19,240 --> 01:25:22,240
Q. Last night you spoke of disorder,

1066
01:25:22,240 --> 01:25:26,240
and when one realises it is disorder,

1067
01:25:26,240 --> 01:25:34,240
and, you know, he can learn, if he looks at disorder,

1068
01:25:34,240 --> 01:25:39,240
and he can find order through that, and learn the discipline,

1069
01:25:39,240 --> 01:25:43,240
and in a way become enlightened, because you are just being aware,

1070
01:25:43,240 --> 01:25:46,240
you're not naming it like when somebody calls you an ass,

1071
01:25:46,240 --> 01:25:48,240
and you become aware.

1072
01:25:48,240 --> 01:25:51,240
But then, why sometimes do people,

1073
01:25:51,240 --> 01:25:53,240
even when they're endowed with this new freshness,

1074
01:25:53,240 --> 01:25:57,240
all of a sudden there's a lack of carrying it out,

1075
01:25:57,240 --> 01:26:02,240
carrying out the action, kind of falls back and becomes stagnant?

1076
01:26:03,240 --> 01:26:05,240
K. You are asking, are you, madame,

1077
01:26:05,240 --> 01:26:09,240
why isn't one enlightened all the time?

1078
01:26:09,240 --> 01:26:11,240
Q. Why?

1079
01:26:11,240 --> 01:26:14,240
K. Isn't that it?

1080
01:26:14,240 --> 01:26:17,240
Q. Well, it seems like it's a ladder.

1081
01:26:17,240 --> 01:26:23,240
K. Why doesn't enlightenment last a long time?

1082
01:26:23,240 --> 01:26:28,240
Why doesn't intelligence function all the time?

1083
01:26:29,240 --> 01:26:33,240
Why does one occasionally become stupid?

1084
01:26:37,240 --> 01:26:41,240
You know, you see, at the end of this talk

1085
01:26:41,240 --> 01:26:45,240
you will go away being violent.

1086
01:26:46,240 --> 01:26:50,240
What's the point of meeting together

1087
01:26:50,240 --> 01:26:56,240
if this remains in your heart and in your mind?

1088
01:26:57,240 --> 01:27:03,240
We spent an hour and a half trying to see what violence is,

1089
01:27:03,240 --> 01:27:10,240
and understanding it and really eliminating it, going beyond it.

1090
01:27:11,240 --> 01:27:16,240
Sir, it's half past twelve. Don't you think we'd better stop?

1091
01:27:16,240 --> 01:27:20,240
Yes, sir. Just one more question, that'll be enough.

1092
01:27:20,240 --> 01:27:25,240
Q. I would like to hear you express yourself.

1093
01:27:25,240 --> 01:27:32,240
You said there you receive energy from violence.

1094
01:27:32,240 --> 01:27:37,240
Isn't the selfless love of one brother to another

1095
01:27:37,240 --> 01:27:41,240
the deadliest weapon in the world

1096
01:27:41,240 --> 01:27:47,240
because of people's total inability to energise themselves in this?

1097
01:27:47,240 --> 01:27:51,240
And can you not take the hate

1098
01:27:51,240 --> 01:27:56,240
and energise that hate and return love?

1099
01:27:56,240 --> 01:27:58,240
K. I don't quite understand, sir.

1100
01:27:58,240 --> 01:28:00,240
Q. I don't quite understand it myself.

1101
01:28:00,240 --> 01:28:04,240
I'm trying to get my head in this place.

1102
01:28:05,240 --> 01:28:09,240
Love, I'm convinced, is the deadliest weapon in the world.

1103
01:28:09,240 --> 01:28:13,240
And when you're coping with a neighbour that's violent,

1104
01:28:13,240 --> 01:28:16,240
can you not take that violence

1105
01:28:16,240 --> 01:28:20,240
and use it as a source of energy to return love?

1106
01:28:20,240 --> 01:28:24,240
K. No, sir, I don't quite see this point.

1107
01:28:24,240 --> 01:28:33,240
Look, sir, I'm your neighbour, you hate me, or I hate you.

1108
01:28:34,240 --> 01:28:40,240
And you say to me, you're asking whether you cannot take my hate

1109
01:28:40,240 --> 01:28:43,240
and turn that energy into love

1110
01:28:43,240 --> 01:28:50,240
and respond to man who hates with love. Is that it?

1111
01:28:50,240 --> 01:28:56,240
Q. When you return love, if the only way you can...

1112
01:28:56,240 --> 01:29:02,240
Really, when I asked this question, I wanted your awareness on this.

1113
01:29:02,240 --> 01:29:08,240
To be able to take violence and hatred and use that as a...

1114
01:29:08,240 --> 01:29:11,240
K. Why should I use it, sir?

1115
01:29:11,240 --> 01:29:13,240
Q. To be able to cope with it.

1116
01:29:13,240 --> 01:29:20,240
K. We dealt with that question just now when the gentleman asked,

1117
01:29:20,240 --> 01:29:24,240
what shall I do if there is no violence in me

1118
01:29:24,240 --> 01:29:28,240
when my neighbour is violent?

1119
01:29:28,240 --> 01:29:31,240
To that we said,

1120
01:29:31,240 --> 01:29:35,240
if you really have no sense of violence,

1121
01:29:35,240 --> 01:29:39,240
then you will know what to do when your neighbour is violent.

1122
01:29:39,240 --> 01:29:45,240
Don't determine now what you will do.

1123
01:29:45,240 --> 01:29:52,240
Don't have a formula for a life which is not violent.

1124
01:29:52,240 --> 01:29:58,240
If you have a formula, then that very formula is breeding violence.

1125
01:29:58,240 --> 01:30:01,240
I think you better stop, sir.
